    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "*Hearing Impairment "
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Hearing loss classified as "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "conductive · sensorineural or both"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " (mixed loss) - "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       },
       {
        "type": "underline",
        "attrs": {
         "style": "single"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "TX"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ": tx underlying cause · hearing aids · cochlear implants · surg "
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "•conductive: disrupted conduction of sound from outer → middle → inner ear · sensorineural: dysfunction of inner ear (cochlea) or CN VIII · auditory neuropathy spectrum dx: abnorm auditory nerve or brainstem response"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "•untx hearing loss in children → affects norm development of speech · language & cognitive skills"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "•"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       },
       {
        "type": "shade",
        "attrs": {
         "hex": "F7CAAC"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "MCC of conductive loss = otitis media"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " - others incl "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       },
       {
        "type": "italic"
       }
      ],
      "text": "cerumen impaction"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " · otitis externa · "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       },
       {
        "type": "italic"
       }
      ],
      "text": "exostoses"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " (bony outgrowths of external auditory canal related to cold H2O exposure) · TM perf · otosclerosis · neoplasms · FB · trauma · congenital malformations · cholesteatoma (growth of stratified squamous epithelium ← repeated ear infect) "
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "•"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       },
       {
        "type": "shade",
        "attrs": {
         "hex": "F7CAAC"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "MCC of sensorineural loss = presbycusis"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " (gradual, symmetrical loss assoc w age) - others incl noise-induced · infect · drug-induced · congenital · Meniere dz · CNS lesions"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "•peds sensorineural causes: congenital (infect · malformations · perilymph fistula) · hereditary (Alport · Hurler · achondroplasia · Marfan · osteogenesis imperfecta · Ehlers-Danlos) · acquired (prematurity · infect · ototoxic drugs · excessive noise · heavy metals (cadmium · mercury · arsenic) · tumors · trauma)"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "•sensorineural = MCC of congenital hearing loss - nonsyndromic genetic causes = large proportion (FHx of same findings + otherwise norm PE) - conductive also ← abnorm formation of auricle or helix · middle ear effusions"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "•infect assoc w sensorineural loss: congenital CMV · bacterial meningitis · TORCH (toxoplasmosis · rubella · syphilis · Zika) - "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "test all infants w sensorineural loss for congenital CMV"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "•ototoxic drugs: aminoglycosides (gentamicin · neomycin) · macrolides · high-dose loop diuretics (furosemide) · chemo (cisplatin · bleomycin) · salicylates"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "•ddx salicylate toxicity: MC causes sensorineural (⍉conductive) loss - salicylate use in peds assoc w Reye syndrome (caution when treating fever or pain) - toxic aspirin dose in peds = 150mg/kg"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "•eval: hx (congenital dx · birth comp · medical conditions · FHx · trauma · offending meds) · PE for anatomic abnorm suggestive of a genetic syndrome · ear exam for infect · FB · scarring · masses → formal audiology if further eval needed"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "•screen: newborn · ages 4 · 5 · 6 · 8 & 10 + once b/n ages 11-14 · 15-17 & 18-21 - AABR · OAE or pure tone tympanometry (>4yo)"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "•abnorm audiology → refer to ENT · speech-language pathology & early intervention"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "•severe-profound sensorineural loss: "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "cochlear implantation"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " most effective tx when hearing correction desired - bypasses damaged cochlear hair cells & directly stimulates auditory nerve via implanted electrode array (vs hearing aids amplify sound) → ↑speech perception · language development · communication - for loss too severe to benefit from hearing aids"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "•confirm profound sensorineural loss w diagnostic audiologic testing → prompt ENT & audiology referral for cochlear implant candidacy - earlier implantation → better language acquisition & long-term communication"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "•not all families elect implantation (deafness as cultural & linguistic identity · ASL) → balanced nonjudgmental counseling (hearing tech · sign language · educational resources · medical & deaf community supports)"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "•conductive loss tx (⍉for sensorineural): myringotomy tubes → recurr or chronic OM · stapedectomy → otosclerosis (stapes fixed to cochlea) · tympanoplasty → repair TM perf"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "•whisper ≈ 20-30 dB"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
